        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Allan Dwan, George Marshall, Aaron Hoffman, Samuel Shipman\n- Works: Friendly Enemies\n- Roles: director, producer, screenwriter, actor, film director, television director, playwright\n\nFacts:\n- Allan Dwan was born on 3 April 1885 and died on 28 December 1981.\n- Allan Dwan was a pioneering Canadian-born American motion picture director, producer, and screenwriter.\n- George E. Marshall was born on December 29, 1891 and died on February 17, 1975.\n- George E. Marshall was an American actor, screenwriter, producer, film director, and television director who was active through the first six decades of movie history.\n- Friendly Enemies was directed by Allan Dwan.\n- Friendly Enemies was adapted from a play of the same name by Aaron Hoffman and Samuel Shipman.",
